  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Saturday/...Active weather looks \nto continue for the long term period with multiple lows moving \ninto the Gulf and subsequently past the panhandle bringing more \nrain and wind to the area. Another circulation looks for move into\nthe area Tuesday night into early Wednesday morning which will \nbring another reinforcing round of moisture and wind. These winds \nwill remain active with the lows passing by the area. Once these \nlows dissipate, we will see a break in the winds for the area for \nThursday before our attention then turns towards the potential of \na low moving up the Aleutian chain and into the western Gulf \nThursday. Current ensemble guidance shows this system crossing the\nGulf Friday into Saturday while higher pressure remains the \nInterior and the Yukon. One thing that will need to be watched is \nif an area of high pressure does develop as some ensemble members \nare hinting at. But at this moment, more members are agreement \nthat a high does not form. The big area of uncertainty is the \nexact track and strength of this low as there is some divergence \nregarding this feature. Getting towards the end of the week, with \nsome of the cooler air spilling over from Canada, it will be more \npossible to see some mixed precipitation for places like Haines \nand Skagway starting Thursday. The Icy Strait corridor could see \nsome mixed potentially for next weekend if the guidance continues \nwith the colder overnight lows and lowered snow levels.",
